1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,080
This is the Wall of Daidatep.

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:03,919
Its signature Cent,

3
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:08,160
number 9908, was struck in 1956,

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,240
carries a full desert patina,

5
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,480
is Faceless, and is contaminated

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,919
with Special Oddities.

7
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:20,000
The Wall holds 132 Cents, from 1944 to 1982,

8
00:00:20,079 --> 00:00:21,120
which puts it in the Dollar

9
00:00:21,199 --> 00:00:23,199
Club, for a hundred Cents or more.

10
00:00:23,679 --> 00:00:25,280
Ten of them are wheat pennies,

11
00:00:25,399 --> 00:00:27,440
minted 1958 or earlier,

12
00:00:27,559 --> 00:00:29,679
with two ears of wheat on the back.

13
00:00:29,719 --> 00:00:32,240
The earliest is from 1944.

14
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:37,039
It holds four Cents from 1971 and four from 1969,

15
00:00:37,119 --> 00:00:40,880
for the 1971 Club and the 1969 Club.

16
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,439
Cent number 3640 is the only

17
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:46,640
Cent from 1955 with a D mint mark,

18
00:00:46,719 --> 00:00:49,039
which makes it a 1/1 Mint.

19
00:00:49,159 --> 00:00:52,159
Four of its Cents are 1/1 Trait Combos:

20
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:53,679
each carries a pair of traits

21
00:00:53,759 --> 00:00:55,600
found on no other Cent.

22
00:00:55,679 --> 00:00:57,759
The signature Cent is one of them.

23
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:00,479
Seven of its Cents carry a full patina:

24
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,320
four full red, two full

25
00:01:02,439 --> 00:01:04,719
obsidian and the full desert.

26
00:01:04,799 --> 00:01:07,040
The Wall completes five Sets.

27
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:08,640
A Spectrum Set:

28
00:01:08,719 --> 00:01:11,439
a significant verdigris, a full obsidian,

29
00:01:11,519 --> 00:01:13,760
a full red, a full desert,

30
00:01:13,799 --> 00:01:15,760
a notable gold and an orange.

31
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,599
A Chronicle Set:

32
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:23,040
a Cent from 1971, from 1979 and from 1982.

33
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:24,640
A Full Mint Set:

34
00:01:24,719 --> 00:01:28,359
an S mint, a D mint and a Cent with no mint mark.

35
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:31,280
Its S mint is from 1945.

36
00:01:31,359 --> 00:01:33,120
A Three Decades Set:

37
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,280
every mint year of the 1960s,

38
00:01:35,359 --> 00:01:38,239
the 1970s and the 1980s.

39
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:40,719
And a Full Contamination Set,

40
00:01:40,799 --> 00:01:43,120
all twelve contamination types:

41
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:46,560
paint, glue, sea salt, scotch tape,

42
00:01:46,719 --> 00:01:49,040
dark grime, obscure adhesive,

43
00:01:49,239 --> 00:01:51,040
blood, unknown liquid,

44
00:01:51,159 --> 00:01:53,200
3D black, speckles,

45
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:56,159
alien secretion and special oddities.

46
00:01:56,239 --> 00:01:59,120
As of October 2026, Daidatep is one

47
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,959
of only two collectors to hold

48
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:04,000
one of these rare Full Contamination Sets.

49
00:02:04,079 --> 00:02:06,319
The Wall carries Diamond Hands:

50
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,080
it has held its position for at least

51
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:10,560
a year, with little to no selling.

52
00:02:10,719 --> 00:02:12,879
And it is a Mint Keeper: Daidatep

53
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,520
minted Cent number 845 and still

54
00:02:15,599 --> 00:02:17,680
holds it, never sold.

